// Over-rejection guard for the unknown-attribute check. Every attribute the compiler gives meaning
// to must keep working — the recognized set is the UNION of what the compiler acts on and what the
// corpus already uses, so failing closed rejects typos and inventions without breaking a working
// program. If this goes red, the whitelist has become the wall.
#[verified]
fn f() -> i64 { return 1; }
fn main() { print(f()); }
